& \Rightarrow \quad \frac{\sec ^2 \theta+\cos ^2 \theta}{2} \geq 1\left[\because \sec \theta=\frac{1}{\cos \theta}\right] \\
& \Rightarrow \quad \sec ^2 \theta+\cos ^2 \theta \geq 2 \Rightarrow f(\theta) \geq 2
\end{aligned}\therefore$ The value of $f(\theta)$ always lies in the interval $[2, \infty)$.

